 "method": "Each GCC ward is sampled on a 25 m grid (finer for wards under 400 samples); each point is placed in a TNGIS revenue village polygon; the village's taluk is TNGIS's own, except Kolathur, Peravallur and Siruvallur, which the Chennai Collectorate lists as the Kolathur taluk formed in 2024. The ward's taluk is the taluk holding the largest share of its area; 'share' is that taluk's share of the whole ward area.",
 "ward_geometry": "chennai-grievance-portal-main/data/boundaries/gcc-wards.geojson",
 "ward_geometry_note": "The ward polygons are the pipeline's (a DataMeet community copy of the GCC wards), so every ward number means the same area here as on the console's map. TNGIS's GCC ward layer follows the zone ranges of the 2021 wards-committee notification (Tamil Nadu Government Gazette Extraordinary No. 594, 14 Dec 2021: zone II = wards 15-22, III = 23-33, XIII = 168-180, XIV = 181-191); the DataMeet file follows the superseded 2011 numbering in several zones. tngis_ward_taluk gives the taluk of the TNGIS ward with the same number, ready for the day the console switches to the official ward polygons (then re-run this script).",
